{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And at Horeb you provoked.</b> This testifies to the evil of the trait of stubbornness, for although you provoked HaShem at Horeb, He would not have said to destroy you except because you are a stiff-necked people, as He said: רָאִיתִי אֶת הָעָם הַזֶּה וְהִנֵּה עַם קְשֵׁה עֹרֶף הוּא, הֶרֶף מִמֶּנִּי וְאַשְׁמִידֵם (Deuteronomy 9:13–14). This is because stubbornness indeed removes all hope of return."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:00.159090350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}